WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
JAMIE: At minimum. Because Rufus's
qualifier is the right one.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.460
RUFUS: A Q1 update is not a Q1
resumption. The update could read:

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:10.621
RUFUS: we need another quarter.

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:14.664
ALEX: Worth holding onto. So what do
security teams actually do with this?

00:00:14.664 --> 00:00:18.527
ALEX: The practical implication is that
if Google's program is being flooded,
your

00:00:18.527 --> 00:00:22.390
ALEX: own vulnerability disclosure
channels face exactly the same pressure.
The tools to

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:26.253
ALEX: generate a plausible-looking
security report are available to anyone
with an internet

00:00:26.253 --> 00:00:30.116
ALEX: connection.
